+// hardware notes, "Mip level selection"; texture_params.x bits 5 and up, set
+// by the renderer): D = log16(g) - log16(q) (auto), the constant (constant) or
+// the constant - log16(q) (slope), the constant holding what does not change
+// across the draw. q is the GE's per-pixel q: 1/w (gl_FragCoord.w) times the
+// texture matrix's q; s and t are the texture coordinates times 1/w, whose
+// screen gradients g takes, in texels of level 0. D is clamped to the levels
+// the texture has; the nearest mip filter takes level (D + 8) >> 4, the linear
+// one blends level D >> 4 with the next by D & 15.
